---
description: Obligatory ruleset
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- NO fallback values - Methods must succeed with real data or throw exceptions
- NO estimation logic - Methods must use actual data sources
- NO simulation comments - Methods must be fully implemented
- NO placeholder behavior - Methods must perform real work
- ONLY real implementations - Methods must use actual system APIs and data sources
- NEVER push to GitHub
- Always follow project XML comments format (bilingual)
- Always add extensive XML documentation to all methods
- Always do Clean before every Build to see clear errors and warnings situation
- Supress only false-positive warnings, all other warnings should be treated as errors
- For CA2227 warnings, avoid using pragma suppressions. Fix them by removing the set accessor or changing it to init, and if replacing a collection, use Clear() and AddRange() instead of reassigning the property.
- Create large files (500+ lines of code) incrementally by adding small (50-350 lines of code) chunks to Target file.